                "dc.identifier.page_to" : [ {
                  "value" : "0",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.repealed" : [ {
                  "value" : "false",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.section_id" : [ {
                  "value" : "106172",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.section_number" : [ {
                  "value" : "150",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.section_page_note" : [ {
                  "value" : "<span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(1) The Central Government, surveyor, or any other person authorised in this behalf, shall have the power to require the master of a vessel to which this Part applies, to give such information as may be required to ensure compliance with the provisions of this Part.<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(2) The surveyor or any other person empowered under sub-section (<i>1</i>), shall have the powers of a civil court while trying a suit under the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908 (5 of 1908), in respect of the following matters, namely:---<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span><span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(a) summoning and enforcing the attendance of any person and examining him on oath;<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span><span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(b) requiring discovery and production of any document;<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span><span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(c) receiving evidence on affidavit;<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span><span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(d) any other matter which is required to be or may be prescribed.<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(3) Any person who refuses or fails to give the information referred to in sub-section (<i>1</i>), shall be liable for a penalty under this Act.<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/>",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.state_id" : [ {
                  "value" : "1",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
